# -------------------------------------------------------------
# The flow reference for multiplier_top -- the measurement the campaign
# was missing.
#
# Everything known about the macro design so far concerns the ESTIMATOR:
# that its spread is ~25%, that an ensemble buys resolution, that
# roworder reads as 7.8% worse. Whether the flow agrees was never
# measured, because at 900s a run the ensemble is expensive.
#
# Sized rather than guessed. The flow's spread on this design is about
# 25% of the achieved period, so s ~ 6%, and resolving roworder's 7.8%
# needs z*s*sqrt(2/k) < 7.8 -- k of about ten. Fifteen leaves margin.
#
# Four variants: base; roworder, whose true functional effect is exactly
# zero and which the estimator calls 7.8% worse; stage1, which the
# estimator cannot distinguish; and stage4, a large effect that serves as
# a positive control -- if the flow and the estimator disagree even there,
# something is wrong with the comparison rather than with the estimator.
# -------------------------------------------------------------

# k=9 rather than 15: at ~8 flow runs an hour, nine perturbations
# already resolve roworder's 7.8% (z*s*sqrt(2/9) ~ 5.7% at s ~ 6%),
# and the extra six would have cost another two hours for margin
# that changes no conclusion.
